  {
   "kind": "interpretation",
   "title": "Explanation and interpretation",
   "sort_order": 9,
   "payload": {
    "sections": [
     {
      "heading": "Question",
      "paragraphs": [
       "Scored in files that have a real outcome, does a DS05 residual axis separate dogs that died, or had complicated disease, beyond what band neutrophils already show?"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "What was done",
      "paragraphs": [
       "The rule chose axis 1 (congruent but not specific (leukocyte)). Its DS05 loadings on the variables each file shares were used as weights: segmented and band neutrophils in S-CB050 (all 141 infected dogs, both cohorts), and segmented and band neutrophils, lymphocytes, monocytes and platelets (haematocrit removed) in S-CB017 day 1 (31 dogs). Cliff's delta, permutation p (stratified by cohort in S-CB050), bootstrap intervals; BH over the 2 primary tests.",
       "Deviation D3: the rule tied between axes 1 and 2 (both congruent but not specific in S-CB050) and the code took axis 1. Axis 2 was scored as a post hoc check A4: in S-CB050 its score correlates +0.99 with the axis-1 score."
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Result",
      "paragraphs": [
       "S-CB050: the score is higher in dogs that died, delta +0.49 (+0.21 to +0.74), p 0.002, q 0.003, 15 died vs 126 survived.",
       "But this restates the published band-neutrophil finding: band neutrophils alone give +0.60 (+0.39 to +0.78); the score correlates +0.81 with bands; after bands are removed the score gives +0.15 (-0.17 to +0.45), p 0.342. The axis adds nothing beyond bands (the risk the package file named).",
       "S-CB017 (B. canis): delta +0.28 (-0.13 to +0.68), q 0.196, 18 complicated vs 13 uncomplicated; detectable effect about 1.05 SD, and WBC is part of the label. Axis 2 weights give +0.04 (-0.34 to +0.45).",
       "MCP-1 does not track the score: S-CB050 cohort 1 rho -0.10 (-0.30 to +0.10), n 97; S-CB017 day 1 rho +0.23 (-0.16 to +0.58), n 31."
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "What this does not show",
      "paragraphs": [
       "The axis was not replicated (experiment SV-09-02), so this is the score of an unreplicated direction. In S-CB050 only two of its twelve variables exist, so the score is a neutrophil sum, not the DS05 axis. Both files are already seen. Died includes euthanasia for poor prognosis. No predictive score was made and no group of dogs is a subtype."
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
